description:
Write a reader and writer for the ini format ImGui uses, that keeps sections it does not understand untouched:

```cpp
struct Section
{
    std::string type;                     // "Window"
    std::string name;                     // "Stones"
    std::vector<std::string> lines;       // the lines inside, as written (without the newline)
};

std::vector<Section> readIni(const std::string& text);
std::string writeIni(const std::vector<Section>& sections);
std::string getValue(const Section& s, const std::string& key);                   // "" if missing
void setValue(Section& s, const std::string& key, const std::string& value);
```

- `readIni`: a section starts with a line `[Type][Name]`. The type and name are between the brackets; the name may itself contain `]` (for example `[Table][0x8A4C2B11,4]`), so the name ends at the **last** `]` of the line. Every following line, up to the next header, belongs to the section, except empty lines, which are dropped. Lines before the first header are ignored. Lines may end with `\r\n`.
- `writeIni`: each section as `[Type][Name]`, then its lines, then one empty line, all separated by `\n`.
- `getValue(s, "Size")`: the text after `=` on the first line that starts with `Size=`.
- `setValue`: replace the first `Key=` line's value, or append `Key=value` if there is none.

